OL,3,GNEWSA'We need to save water tower
OL,4,Abefore it's too late'
OL,5,
OL,6,FCampaigners hoping to save a Grade II
OL,7,Flisted water tower known as the "iron
OL,8,Fgiant" say time is ticking until it
OL,9,Fbecomes too damaged to rescue.
OL,11,FThe 55m (180ft) landmark, built in
OL,12,F1928, ceased operation in 2006 but
OL,13,Fremains a much-loved sight, with
OL,14,Fresidents trying to secure its
OL,15,Flong-term future amid its deteriorating
OL,16,Fcondition.
OL,18,FBut campaigners say owner Yorkshire
OL,19,FWater has so far not co-operated with
OL,20,Fattempts to restore the tower in time
OL,21,Ffor its centenary in 2028.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
